for (init; cond; increment)

The "init" is the initial value of the loop counter.  In this case, it’s just 0.  The "cond" is an expression that is true when the counter is zero, and false otherwise.  In this case, it’s just the variable "a".  The "increment" is an expression that sets the value of the counter to one more than the current value.  In this case, it’s just "a++".  The loop will run as long as "cond" is true.  When it’s false, the loop counter is set to one more than the current value, and the code performs the action.

